# The harness's text files keep LF in every checkout. corpus.py writes its JSON with LF, and T22 holds
# those files to a fresh run byte for byte. The raw sha256 of each file corpus.py reads from here goes
# into weak_spots.json's sources. Binary files (fixtures) are not named, so nothing converts them.
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
